Patch 2070 (fix line): a vertex program seen for the first time is compiled on a worker thread instead of on the
drawing thread (VS_ASYNC=0 off).

vp_get_vs decompiled and compiled a new vertex program right where the draw was recorded, on the drawing thread, and
D3DCompile takes 100-400 ms for J-Stars' programs: the game froze for a moment when something new appeared (the
maintainer, 11-11: breaking things, turning the camera in a map with many buildings). HITCH and HZC logs of a 2v2 on
Hidden Leaf: the two long frames (306 and 326 ms) were the frames right after a guest_vp2 shader-cache miss
(bench/exp/2026-11-11_1632-breakhitch1); the second run, with those programs cached, had none
(2026-11-11_1637-breakhitch2). Now a program whose text is not in shader_cache.bin gets its slot at once, marked
pending, and two worker threads compile it; until it is ready the draws that use it are skipped (as patch 2057 does
for fragment programs), so the game goes on. A slot reused before its compile ends drops the late result.

Tested (US disc, auto-pilot 2v2 Free Battle on Hidden Leaf, empty shader cache): 57 vertex and 248 fragment programs compiled during the run, no drawing-thread stall over 55 ms in the fight (FTL draw max), picture normal (bench/exp/2026-11-11_1647-vsasync-cold).

